Gale-Shapley — Key Statements
Men propose in preference order.
Women keep the better proposal.
Once engaged, a woman never becomes free.
A woman's partners get better over time.
If rejected, a man proposes to his next choice.
A rejected man cannot propose to the same woman again.
The algorithm stops when everyone is matched.
Men move down their list; women move up their list.


Matching

A matching is a set of pairs where each person is matched with at most one person from the other group.

Example:

m1↔w2
m2↔w1
m3↔w3
Stable Matching

A stable matching is a matching where there is no blocking pair.

A blocking pair is a man and woman who:

are not matched with each other, and
both prefer each other over their current partners.

Easy to remember:

Matching = everyone gets a partner.
Stable matching = no two people would rather be with each other.
